WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.150
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.200
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.260
Within this scattered time

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.560
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.880
We believed you

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.410
The SDF Navy's newest AEGIS class vessel, Mirai.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.450
Sets off from the Yokosuka Base.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.500
But, as she entered the Pacific Ocean...

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.080
Mirai encountered abnormal atmospheric conditions.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.460
She was thrown back in time to June 4th, 1942.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.800
Into the midst of the Battle of Midway.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.510
Caught in the midst of an ongoing war...

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:05.180
What should we do in this era?

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.940
We have yet to find the answer.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.530
0255.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.870
Captain, it's time.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.990
Begin attack!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.450
Commence attack now!

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.590
The Land of Gold

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.720
Five... four... three... two... one.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.720
Lights on!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.370
A warning to Major General Vandegrift!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:13.170
At 3 today, we will launch an attack on the supplies.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.170
We will be using a missile.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.260
A weapon that far surpasses the technology of this era.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.800
Before we take the lives of your officers...

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.760
...we will remove the bread and pancakes from your breakfast.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.760
This is a firm request...

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.020
...and a demonstration requiring the removal of US troops.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.390
The operation is named Sagittarius.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.950
- Send word! Emergency call!
- Right away!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.700
Everyone retreat 600 yards from the supply area!

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.950
- Hurry up!
- Yes sir!

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.550
Contact each unit's radar!

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.970
Beware of contact from unidentified vessel!

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.680
Yes sir!

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.220
Two minutes to 0300.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.350
I don't hear any explosion.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.400
So it's a bluff after all?

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.380
What's that?!

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.890
It's approaching!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.470
Time to contact, 15 seconds! Here it comes!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.430
I see it!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.900
Alright, be a good boy and please stay on course!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.740
General! The sky to the west!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.110
What?!

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.950
Retreat now! Get down!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.670
Yes!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.420
Well done there, Enomoto!

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.210
That went well.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.220
I never thought this fella would come in handy here.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.220
This makes our risky landing worth the effort.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.930
All that time under the raining bombshells didn't go to waste.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.730
Sagittarius hit the bull's eye.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.230
The Harpoon has hit the target.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.990
W-what's that? When did they appear?!

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.950
They avoided our radar because of their proximity to Malaita!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.790
Water Surface Radar has picked up an object!

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.000
30 degrees, 25 miles.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.000
It's a large vessel. Proceeding north at 25 knots!

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Approaching at high speed!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.990
What? It's a dud?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.240
An American ship?

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.580
Or has the Eighth Division decided to turn back again?

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.000
Mikawa's Fleet has 8 vessels.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.290
And the direction is different.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:44.210
The US fleet should've retreated far south.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.010
It's an unexpected situation.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.130
Shall I tell the landing party to pull out?

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.930
Verify the situation first!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.890
Captain, I think we should send out a helicopter.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.970
It's risky, but we've got no other choice.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.480
Permission granted!

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.190
One aircraft preparing for takeoff!

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.530
We've just finished the maintenance.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.280
Sure is hectic during wartime.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.420
Take off!

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.840
The appearance of a fleet that's not recorded in history?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.340
What's going on here?!

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.850
It might have delayed explosion! Stay away from it!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.860
Call in the bomb squad now!

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.280
It's some kind of rocket?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:56.330
It almost had a will of it's own, and pinpointed the flour.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.200
Could this be the mysterious sonar-equipped torpedo?

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.500
So it wasn't a myth after all?

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.750
Major General Vandegrift!

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.970
There's another message for you!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.550
The demonstration is over.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.560
This is a request for Major General Vandegrift.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.520
And the 11000 Marines on shore.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:25.350
By daybreak today, before 0430.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.360
You must pull out all troops and retreat from this beach.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.820
If you do not comply...

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.360
The Arrow of Sagittarius will be targeted at your camp...

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.820
...on Guadalcanal Beach.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:40.330
It will be carrying 220 kilos of TNT.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.910
I have no doubt that you've realised...

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:46.080
...that this is God's arrow, and never misses its mark.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.000
The enemy knows our every move?!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.670
Are we being watched?

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.510
The hills must be crawling with Japanese soldiers!

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.510
Our smooth landing turned out to be a trap after all!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.060
But that thing flew in from the sea!

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.520
There must be a Japanese fleet at sea!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.810
Silence!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.690
This is a war, not a game.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:13.740
Why do they send us warnings and threats?

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:14.990
The answer is simple!

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.870
They want to crush our morale, and confuse us!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.240
Send word to all ships!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.290
Search the surrounding area!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.120
Look for an unidentified fleet!

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.130
Form a scouting unit!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.250
The only person who can order us to retreat...

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.880
...is the President of the United States! Don't forget that!

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.050
Yes sir!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.600
If they have the advantage, why not launch an attack?

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.310
Why give us the chance to retreat?

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:50.440
Are they really with the Japanese?

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:00.910
Navy Self-Defense Force

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.630
Fortune Inspector, visual contact with target.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.050
Speed is unchanged. Heading: Zero, Eight, Two.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.840
Closing in.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.880
Distance with heli, 7 miles.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.800
Sending zoom image now.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.980
Modifying image!

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.870
H-How come?!

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.180
Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.930
Can you swear on your life?

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.390
Can you swear to God?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.520
That you've chosen the right path?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:42.220
The Yamato?! Wasn't it docked at Truk?!

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.100
A message has come in from Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.430
What?!

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.730
The attack fleet, led by Admiral Yamamoto.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:54.900
At 0430 today, will commence...

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.190
...heavy shelling of Guadalcanal.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:02.200
Objective: extermination of the First Marine Division on shore.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:07.660
Mirai's landing party are to move to the southern coast now.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.370
Or pull out at once.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.420
To: SDF Mirai.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:17.380
From: Takumi Kusaka!

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.600
Kusaka!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.900
The American camp's getting busy.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:43.070
If they retreat as planned, then no one will die.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.910
Fortune Inspector.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.410
Everything is progressing smoothly here.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.080
Yosuke. The situation's changed.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.120
Something unexpected has happened.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.460
The Yamato is here?

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.250
Don't be ridiculous! Yamato's at Truk right now!

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.880
It's heading a fleet of twelve, and is currently...

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.430
...24 miles northeast of Red Beach.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.590
They sent us a warning at 0340.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.260
A warning from the Yamato?

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:15.190
At 0430, the Yamato will begin shelling Guadalcanal...

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.560
...to exterminate the US Marines.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.990
The message came from...

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.740
...Takumi Kusaka.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.500
Comman-

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.090
Now you've done it.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.770
Report from the radio room!

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:59.810
0400. At present... no reply from Mirai!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:05.240
Do we proceed to bomb if they don't reply?

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.990
Lieutenant Kusaka, what's next?

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:16.000
No, they will definitely send a reply.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.420
Very well.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.420
Relay order to ships to attack.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.050
Yes!

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.010
Port side! Cannons ready!

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.890
Target: Guadalcanal North Shore.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:35.220
80 degrees port, 30 degree angle!

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:00.620
Yamato's 46cm primary guns...

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:03.790
...have a destructive force that would shock even our era.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:09.010
The Imperial Navy's Type 1 Bomber carries 800 kg bomb.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.050
But Yamato's Type 3 bombs each weigh 1.36 tonnes.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.560
If she fires all 900 rounds...

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:18.060
It would be equivalent to 1500 Type One bombs.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.310
What's more, the bombs are designed to pierce armour...

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.820
...so trenches are useless against it.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.570
Red Beach won't be the only thing to change...

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.900
...even this island may not keep its shape.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:37.540
We may be at war, but this constitutes a massacre...

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.710
...of defenseless opponents.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.840
Fortune Inspector.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.380
Captain, I need to speak with you.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.720
A report! We have a reply from Mirai!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.430
So it's finally arrived.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.010
The Mirai will not recognize the Yamato...

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.350
...or her fleet's intended attack on Allied Troops.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:03.560
None of the men currently positioned on Guadalcanal...

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.980
...that is, Commander Kadomatsu and his three subordinates...

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.360
...have any intention of retreating.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.860
What's that? What does that mean?

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:14.870
Rear Admiral Ugaki! We have 10 minutes before bombing!

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.870
What should we do now?

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.540
Captain Kuroshima.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:26.290
How long does it take to get to the rear deck from here?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.710
For me, it's a 10 minute walk. But if you run...

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:32.930
...it would only take 4 to 5 minutes.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.930
- Why do you ask?
- It's nothing.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.890
Thank you very much.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:01.680
Commander Kadomatsu.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:05.430
I hope you can hear my voice.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.640
If you can hear me, I hope you will reply.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:10.810
Kusaka! Where're you calling from?

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.780
From the Umidori inside Yamato's hanger deck.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.860
Where is Lieutenant Satake?

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.660
Don't tell me you...

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.330
He's being treated as a guest on this ship.

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.450
There's no need for worry.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.540
That aside, Commander Kadomatsu...

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.330
...please hear me out.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.540
Why should I?

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:34.210
All your big talk about stopping the operations...

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.510
...was a lie!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:41.470
The plan to pull the Japanese out of the Pacific isn't a lie!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.770
We are, however, fighting a war!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:48.560
I believed I would have your understanding in this matter.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.270
The bombing will commence in 5 minutes.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.770
I don't want you to die!

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.440
Just go ahead and try!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.690
Mirai will do her best to stop Yamato!

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.280
Are you on the American's side?

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:03.370
To the Mirai, the blood of all people are the same!

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:05.290
All of it is red!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:09.370
The dignity of human life is not based on country or race.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.540
You're right about that, Commander Kadomatsu.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:15.550
I believe that your words have saved me.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:16.340
What?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:21.390
That a ranking Japanese officer, just 60 years from now.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:24.810
Thinks the way you do, makes me very proud.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.890
But, that is morality in peace-time.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.730
Unfortunately, we're in a time of war.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.190
It's a sad truth but...

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.860
Soldiers or civilians, all of Japan is at war.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:41.030
This was all caused by the militarists of Imperial Japan.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.360
And you are one of them!

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.070
That's no longer true.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:47.240
After meeting you, and knowing the future.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:51.500
I have come to realize the mistake made by my country.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.460
I have returned my sword to Admiral Yamamoto,

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.800
So I'm no longer a military personnel.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:01.430
As regards the members of Mirai embroiled in this war...

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.890
Imperial Japan isn't the country they should be protecting.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.060
The motherland you swore to protect...

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.390
...disappeared in the fog on that fateful day.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:13.650
Well, then you should understand our cause, right?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.570
Soldiers exist to protect their people...

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.400
...their assets, and the country's sovereignty.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.610
They do not exist to protect humanistic ideals.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.740
As I guessed, you're nothing but an imperial soldier...

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:27.120
...out to massacre the American troops!

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.830
You're wrong! We have to fight on.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.750
...because there's another country we need to protect.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.040
Is there such a country?!

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.000
Yes!

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.170
I'm not talking about the Great Japanese Empire.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.970
Who thoughtlessly threw herself into this war.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:45.760
And I don't mean post-war Japan.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.810
Who surrenders unconditionally, and is shamed.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.720
After knowing both countries...

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:53.770
A new country...

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.270
...has taken shape in my mind.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:11.580
An independent island, surrounded by the sea.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.040
And brimming with strength...

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.000
...is standing right before our eyes.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:24.300
It's name is Zipang.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.970
Zipang you say?

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.060
Yes, we'll call her that.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:40.150
That was the name the western travelers once used.

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:44.190
It's going to be a new country, however...

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:47.490
...one that even the Japan of your era has not seen before.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.960
Zipang. I have no doubt that you can see it too.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:00.170
Zipang.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:17.200
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:22.440
Just peacefully

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:34.220
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:47.130
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:53.730
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:59.810
I kept on praying

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:11.650
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:27.340
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:42.390
Kusaka's serious about it.

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:44.810
The Yamato will carry out the attack.

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:46.730
The Yamato's main guns are very rapid.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.810
If we don't act quickly we won't be able to stop them.

00:23:48.810 --> 00:23:52.270
I'd like the Mirai to fight alongside me!

00:23:52.270 --> 00:23:56.400
I never thought the Mirai would be Yamato's first opponent.

00:23:56.820 --> 00:23:58.320
Bring it on!

00:23:58.320 --> 00:24:01.070
We will take you down along with the Yamato!

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:04.950
Next Episode: Collision!

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:04.870
You're finally bearing your fangs, Mirai.

